WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
- But what's been the
most random inspiration

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.020
for a song that you've written.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.660
- Ooh.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.540
There's a song on my second
album called Bad at Love,

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.540
and the song is about me failing miserably

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.550
at like, a bunch of relationships
that's what it's about.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.380
But the inspiration for writing it

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.340
was I've always wanted a motorcycle

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.690
and I'm way too scared to ride one,

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.280
and I'll never have one.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.650
I just always picture myself getting to.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.370
And so, when I was making the album,

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:34.720
I was like, I want a music
video where I'm on a motorcycle.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.970
I was like, and I want the song

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.660
to sound like a song who'd be like,

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.630
cruising down the road,

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.730
like on your motorcycle,
like listening to.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.630
And just with your hands
in the air, just like.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.190
And somehow, that turned into Bad at Love.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.003
I don't know, it doesn't
make any sense at all, but.

00:00:52.003 --> 00:00:52.836
- It does.

00:00:52.836 --> 00:00:54.510
- It was the inspiration
for the sound of it.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.740
Yeah.
- No, I'm like that

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.380
almost whenever I write a song as well.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:58.610
I have to have imagery.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:00:59.920
Like I must have a video playing,

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.500
like while I'm writing in my head.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.720
How do you deal,

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:04.560
like when you're writing,

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.720
how do you deal with writer's block?

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.020
If you're like needing to cut,

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.450
like you're working on an
album for whatever reason,

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:09.300
you're just like blocked.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.510
How do you do that?

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:12.150
- Oh, usually, it's by doing something

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.420
like super regrettable,

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.413
like cutting bangs or
like piercing my nose.

00:01:16.413 --> 00:01:17.902
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:17.902 --> 00:01:19.035
- Super regrettable.

00:01:19.035 --> 00:01:21.630
(both laughing)

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:24.120
- Usually that's what I do. It's like,

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.310
there's three things I do.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:29.430
It's I dye my hair or cut bangs,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:33.965
I get a tattoo, or I call
an ex for closure and.

00:01:33.965 --> 00:01:36.423
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:36.423 --> 00:01:39.650
- Only two work out well. So, you know.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:40.870
(crowd clapping)

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.210
- I love her so much.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.043
She's so cool.

00:01:43.043 --> 00:01:44.460
Halsey and I talked a lot about

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.330
her New York times bestselling book,

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.390
I Would Leave Me If I Could,

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:49.440
which is I still say
one of the best titles

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.830
I've ever heard in my life.

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.640
She had some really powerful
reasons for writing it.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.220
Take a look at this
previously unseen conversation

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.000
about her influences
in the writing process.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:01:59.980
What you actually, you,

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.010
you said that you're close with your mom

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.590
and you dedicated your book to your mom.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:05.270
So, you said you used
to sneak in and this is,

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:06.860
I have a problem with this,

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.690
you used to read her journal?

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.110
- Okay. So, it wasn't
like her personal journal.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.480
It was like her poetry journal.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.797
- Oh, okay. 'Cause I was like,

00:02:13.797 --> 00:02:15.743
"We should talk about that."

00:02:15.743 --> 00:02:17.122
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:17.122 --> 00:02:18.530
- No, it wasn't like I have been beating

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.340
her personal space kinda thing.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.230
Even though there's probably nothing in it

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.950
that she wouldn't have already told me

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.540
'cause she used to tell me
everything like too much, okay?

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.950
My mom used to tell me too much.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.387
Like there's some things
that I would be like,

00:02:29.387 --> 00:02:31.980
"Mom, okay. Like, still your kid.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:32.880
Don't need to know that."

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.600
'Cause we really are best friends.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.930
But it was her poetry journal

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:39.150
and she wrote some of the
most beautiful poetry ever.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:43.320
And then just always wanted
to write as wonderful as her.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.320
And it was really cool
'cause it showed me,

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:47.153
when we're growing up,

00:02:47.153 --> 00:02:49.920
I think we get to know our
parents as just our parents

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.820
and we forget that they're
like really complex people

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:55.880
who have had like their
heartbroken before.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.740
And like they wonder
about other relationships

00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.820
and how their life would have gone

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.330
if things had been different,

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.130
like regret, sadness.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:04.967
And it's so much more than just like,

00:03:04.967 --> 00:03:08.020
"That's my mom. That's all
she is, is just my mom."

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.930
And so I, it made me understand her

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.440
as like more complex of a person,

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.960
and I think it made us closer.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.230
So, I'm definitely
super grateful for that.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.580
- Yeah. That's, we do forget that.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:19.730
And then when you get, as we get older,

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.470
you start to realize,

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.480
especially that they do,

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.377
they had their own lives and
you start to wonder like,

00:03:24.377 --> 00:03:26.940
"What would they have
been like at like 20."

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.380
But how, how would you
describe the feeling

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.130
of needing to write something?

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:33.040
'Cause that's the only way I write.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.210
Like I, usually, all my songs

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:36.300
are when I have to get something out.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.450
- I think I sit on things
for a really long time

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.510
and then I start to feel
like really anxious,

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:42.040
and I can't figure out why.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.150
And then usually, it's
'cause I need to like,

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.950
dig up some feeling that's
deep down inside me.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.860
I mean, Kelly, you are one
of the greatest songwriters

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.870
like ever to ever live.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:52.703
- You're lying.

00:03:52.703 --> 00:03:55.090
- I'm a huge, I'm serious.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.640
I'm a huge fan of your writing.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.130
I'm massively inspired by it.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:02.110
It's so rare in this
industry that there are women

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:05.110
who are performers and entertainers,

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.540
who actually write their own words

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:09.730
and like are determined
to get on the stage,

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:12.240
and sing words that they wrote themselves

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.390
from their own experiences.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.980
And be open about things
that aren't pretty

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.870
or complimentary of themselves,

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.260
or the experiences
they've had that are like,

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.670
you know, sometimes really tough.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:25.470
And like you've always been
that person and that's huge,

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:26.750
huge inspiration for me.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.040
So, like definitely wanting
to make sure I got the chance

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.420
to say that while I'm in front of you.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:31.850
- No, I, actually,

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:33.340
that's a good segue question

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:34.850
because I, it's so funny

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:35.927
'cause people have said that to me like,

00:04:35.927 --> 00:04:38.810
"Oh, is it that hard how honest you are?"

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:40.700
It's not. Like, I think I came out.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.947
I think, it's not hard for me to say,

00:04:42.947 --> 00:04:44.520
"Oh, this happened to me and it sucked.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.040
And this happened to me and whatever."

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:49.480
Like, cause I feel like we all
go through experiences, like.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.770
And nobody's got it, but you know,

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:52.870
everybody's life is different.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:54.440
Everything is valid, every situation.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.760
We all get hurt, we all get shunned.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.450
You know, we all get happy about things.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:00.590
Like, do you, do you have a problem?

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:02.980
Like when you write such personal things,

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.910
does it come naturally
for you to release it?

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.270
Like or does it make
kinda make you scared?

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:09.180
'Cause you're like, "Oh, I don't know

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.670
if I should have been that open."

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.360
- Oh, I think it's always natural,

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:13.887
but then there's always
that kind of moment of like,

00:05:13.887 --> 00:05:15.570
"Oh my gosh, what have I just done?"

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:17.797
'Cause I'll always get really
confident and I'll be like,

00:05:17.797 --> 00:05:19.570
"Yeah, I need to share
this with the world.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.930
And there's other people who've
been through this experience

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.340
and like, they need to know

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.640
that we're all in this together."

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.757
And then I'll put it out and be like,

00:05:26.757 --> 00:05:28.830
"Oh, my God. What did I just do?"

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:30.410
And then usually it ends up being okay

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.780
'cause my fans are wonderful and they're,

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:34.710
they love me so unconditionally.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.020
And they're so good at this point

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.020
about receiving personal information

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.430
because I've always been very honest

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:45.350
and I'm always been like
really avid about sharing,

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:48.050
you know, intimate experiences with them

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:51.000
and they're forgiving and gentle about it.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.780
But you know, if I've ever had experiences

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:55.840
where I've had, you know,

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.820
I've worried about regret,

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:01.250
I always remember, for all the people who

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.010
their voices seem negative,

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:04.790
there's so many more people out there

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:08.750
who are sharing with me
that they've been helped by.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.497
You know, my, by me sharing my experience

00:06:11.497 --> 00:06:14.890
and that makes it worth
it always, every time.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.680
You know? I'm sure you feel the same.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:17.513
- Yeah, no, and I.

00:06:17.513 --> 00:06:19.200
It's so funny that my first song

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.700
that was like super personal,

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:21.760
I remember putting it out and
I was kind of nervous about it

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.100
'cause I was like, "Oh,
it's pretty personal."

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.040
And then after that experience,

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.010
I think like you said,

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:31.140
like even if you like connect
with one random person

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:32.500
that could be and like,

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.950
you know, Thailand or whatever

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.790
that really needed that song
that you were a vessel for,

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:39.980
like that's the coolest
thing ever as an artist.

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:41.110
And I just wondered if it was,

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:43.570
it's not always easy for
everybody to be so open

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:46.360
and it actually ended up
becoming very natural for me

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.640
'cause I think I'm naturally
like that and in general.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:49.550
And I've seen you in interviews

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.270
and that's what I love about you.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.900
You're kind of an open book,

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:53.870
whether it's your poetry,

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:54.703
whether it's painting,

00:06:54.703 --> 00:06:55.780
with just how you are.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.860
You're just like, "This is me
and it's cool if you like it.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.630
And if you don't, that's cool too."

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:00.900
And I think that that's admirable.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:01.733
Like you don't have your card,

00:07:01.733 --> 00:07:03.920
you can actually wrote
all this in a card too

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.010
that I write to every guest
that comes to the show

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:06.900
because I love that.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.790
It's, we need strong, powerful women,

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.250
especially for little girls

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.270
and for little boys to see powerful women

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:14.300
in those positions, you know?

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.243
And, and to create that norm.

